 ### [Parallel Octree Data Reduction](16751-parallel-octree-data-reduction.md)
-A technique for interactive visualization of large scientific datasets that combines hierarchical data reduction with parallel computing. It builds on Round-robin Leaf Assignment by providing the data structure and reduction logic that precedes or accompanies the distribution strategy. Unlike uniform grid subsampling, it places more points where data changes rapidly to minimize approximation error. When to choose it: Not given in the sources.
+A technique for the interactive visualization of large scientific datasets by combining hierarchical data reduction with parallel computing. It distributes data across Massively Parallel Processing (MPP) processors to build a distributed-memory octree, allowing users to interactively adapt resolution (refine or prune) on a local graphics workstation while retaining access to full-resolution data. Unlike uniform grid subsampling, which uses a fixed grid and allows more grid points but higher approximation error in complex regions, this method places more points where data changes rapidly to minimize approximation error. It builds on [Round-robin Leaf Assignment](12287-round-robin-leaf-assignment.md) by providing the data structure and reduction logic that precedes or accompanies the distribution strategy. When to choose it: Not given in the sources.
 
